#: inc/admin/theme-page.php:55
msgid "Structured data, meta tags, breadcrumbs, the accessibility corrections for core blocks and for WooCommerce, the visitor display settings and the login screen. Ships with the theme. Without it the templates still render, but the breadcrumb block is missing and no structured data is emitted."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-page.php:61
msgid "Contact and enquiry forms. It ships almost no styling by design, so the theme supplies the submit button, the field widths and the validation colours. Those rules load only where Contact Form 7 has loaded its own stylesheet."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-page.php:67
msgid "Contact forms with a drag and drop builder. It exposes its design through custom properties, which the theme maps onto its own colours, corner radii and the 44 pixel minimum target size. Anything you restyle in the WPForms settings still wins."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-page.php:73
msgid "Selling. The theme stops WooCommerce opening a second main landmark on shop pages, brings its buttons and the show password toggle up to the minimum target size, and styles its tables, notices and checkout fields."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-page.php:79
msgid "Consent banner. Basalt Core repairs the contrast of its accept and reject labels: the plugin paints those buttons in a colour from its own settings and leaves the label white, and its default gives 2.93 to 1 where 4.5 is required. Your colour is left alone, only the label moves."
msgstr ""

#: inc/admin/theme-page.php:85
msgid "Editorial control over titles, descriptions and redirects. Basalt Core detects it and steps out of the way, so nothing is emitted twice. Rank Math, SEOPress, All in One SEO, Slim SEO and Squirrly are recognised in the same way."
msgstr ""

